+# patches/
+
+dsh-side (harness) patches this plugin still needs on the `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`
+corridor. They are applied on top of a clean checkout of
+`https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness` at tag `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`;
+the checkout under `.dsh-migrate/harness` carries both, uncommitted.
+
+| Patch | Harness files | Why the plugin needs it |
+|---|---|---|
+| [`0001-client-slot-shadow-child-declaration.patch`](0001-client-slot-shadow-child-declaration.patch) | `packages/client/ui-slots/src/index.ts` | The slot catalog documents `single` cells as replacement points (and the browser-half facade auto-assigns third-party registrations a lower priority), but a replacement cannot declare a child hole the shadowed entry already declares, and without the declaration it is not authorized to render that hole. Without the handoff, replacing the workspace browser means disabling the whole official `ui-workspace` row — which removes the `ctx.uiWorkspace` service official surfaces inject, so the replacement must reimplement navigation policy. |
+| [`0002-session-projcache-per-unit-rows.patch`](0002-session-projcache-per-unit-rows.patch) | `packages/session/session-projection-cache/src/index.ts` | The persisted projection cache validates the whole per-session record at once; a single unit state that is not losslessly JSON drops every cold row of that session (titles included — [discussion #3183](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/3183) is the upstream request, [#5772](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5772) the symptom report). The patched `put()` validates per projection key, drops only the offending row with one warning, and keeps the previous record when every row fails. The plugin's host fallback writes `session_projcache` directly only because no official seam seeds or repairs one cold row. |
+
+Apply / verify (run from this repository's root; `git -C` resolves a relative
+patch path against the checkout, so pass an absolute one):
+
+```sh
+git -C .dsh-migrate/harness apply "$PWD/patches/0001-client-slot-shadow-child-declaration.patch"
+git -C .dsh-migrate/harness apply "$PWD/patches/0002-session-projcache-per-unit-rows.patch"
+node patches/tests/ui-slots-shadow-child-declaration.test.mjs
+node patches/tests/projection-cache-partial-checkpoint.test.mjs
+node tests/workspace-root-hook.test.mjs
+```
+
+The tests load the touched harness sources directly through Node's TypeScript
+type stripping (the checkout has no installed dependencies). Each harness-side
+test fails on the pristine tree in the way its patch fixes; see the per-patch
+reports under `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/` for before/after output and the
+upstream discussion search.
